CORE no-new-smt
main.c
--isolate-properties
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ not one: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ functional consistency: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The constraints for the functional consistency of uninterpreted functions are
added when the solver is first run, which is under the assumption that the
first property fails. They must nevertheless hold for all later solver calls.
